# Flap Fit launch readiness — September 17, 2026

The launch goal is blocked pending owner approvals and real-device evidence; it is not complete. No Apple, Google Play, or Shipaton submission has been made.
Use this status with the physical test matrix; older dated audit notes describe earlier candidates.

## Implemented and checked

- The approved sharing and ad packages are installed at their approved versions. iOS Messages and
  Mail use native composers; social sharing still uses the system share sheet and the full video file.
  The user confirmed full-duration text delivery, correct video duration and audio, and long iPhone
  Snapchat clips. No claim is made that a receiving social app automatically returns control.
- Fixed the iOS attachment type bug in the approved expo-sms 57.0.2 source using a checked-in
  Yarn patch. Apple's composer now receives the computed UTI instead of a MIME string. Yarn's
  immutable install passed; only the SMS patch entry changed in the existing dependency graph.
  Expo Go retains the complete-file system share path because its bundled native SDK cannot use
  this patch. The native Messages shortcut still requires an installed-build send/cancel test.
- Ads are eligible only after Done, Try Again, or Next Level, with the app foregrounded and sharing
  finished. First exit is free, at most one ad per two exits, at least 90 seconds between displays.
  Result arrival, a share callback, and returning to the foreground do not trigger ads.
- Consent setup cannot open a late form over active gameplay. Native ads are skipped in Expo Go;
  preview uses test units, production uses the configured live units. SDK failure and unavailable
  ads preserve the selected result action. A started native presentation waits for close/failure
  rather than navigating under a delayed ad.
- RevenueCat manual AdTracker integration sends ad lifecycle/revenue events with a separate
  anonymous identifier. It does not receive camera, fitness, score, player-name, or challenge data.
  No purchases, subscriptions, paywalls, or remove-ads product were added.
- Both Flap Fit AdMob apps and result-exit interstitials exist. Impression-level ad revenue is on.
  European and US privacy messages are saved drafts for the two Flap Fit apps. European refusal is
  enabled in all regions. Ad partner settings are account-wide and were not changed; the account
  also contains another app. Google states those partners can apply to non-personalized ads too.
- New challenge codes save the selected exercise and pipe-score target. Opening one uses its saved
  exercise regardless of the lobby. The server rejects mismatched attempts. Level 3 is retained;
  challenges were not silently changed to Endless. Three existing codes remain Any exercise.
  Sharing a saved code uses its saved target, so editing the next draft cannot change its message.
- The lobby onboarding-preview button is removed. First-use onboarding and Info access remain.
  Top-50 exercise leaderboards and the hidden Sky-mode camera preview are retained.

## Verification evidence

- Full mobile Jest after the iOS attachment patch and Expo Go routing guard: **24 suites,
  176 tests passed**. TypeScript and strict oxlint passed. This includes the PG re-consent regression.
- Yarn immutable install passed. Installed native source uses the correct UTI; the patch is included
  by EAS source rules; the lockfile has no unrelated dependency changes. The pre-existing staged
  Git patch still matches its saved baseline. These checks do not substitute for Swift compilation.
- Live API: all six challenge exercise bindings passed create/read/matching-run/wrong-exercise
  checks; invalid input was rejected; old clients still work. Terms, run timing, replay protection,
  idempotent retries, and deletion also passed. Temporary test profile deletion returned 200.
  Post-test database query confirmed zero LaunchTest profiles and exactly three original codes.
- `flapfit-game` version **6** is active with JWT verification enabled. Additive exercise migration
  is live. Local file: `20260917072007_bind_challenges_to_exercise.sql`; hosted version:
  `20260917072148`. Earlier local/hosted timestamps also differ; names match. Do not blindly run
  a CLI database push against this history.
- Public tables have RLS and deny direct client access. Privileged RPCs, including the new one,
  deny anon/authenticated execution. Cron schema usage is denied to both roles. Security advisors
  still list generic Cron policies and disabled leaked-password protection; the app uses anonymous
  auth without a password flow. These are recorded rather than hidden or called fixed.
- Production-environment native configuration inspection passed: correct bundle/app IDs, delayed
  AdMob measurement, no ATT description, 50 SKAdNetwork entries, blocked Android advertising-ID
  and AdServices ID/attribution permissions.
- Current production-environment JavaScript exports passed for both platforms after the SMS
  patch, sharing guard, challenge binding, PG fix, and Android RevenueCat configuration. iOS:
  3,724 modules / 106 assets; Android: 3,818 modules / 110 assets. Input fingerprints were unchanged
  across export. Logs, bundle hashes, and evidence are in current-bundles under the local audit
  folder. These are local bundles, not native builds, device tests, or store uploads.
- Latest Expo Doctor: **20/21 checks passed**. Node's schema fetch failed, but the unchanged
  official SDK 57 schema response downloaded through verified PowerShell HTTPS passed the same
  validator. The transport fallback is logged explicitly; other checks remain unchanged. The only
  finding is the three reviewed Expo patch recommendations. No warnings were excluded.
- Four public release pages passed HTTPS/content checks. Public policy copy still needs the
  prepared advertising update; working URLs do not prove accurate disclosures.

## Remaining launch gates

1. **Pull-up and exercise acceptance:** physically test Form Test 2026-09-16.9 on iPhone/iPad and
   Android, including planted feet, calf raises, actual hanging/reps, full lockout, close shoulder
   press with elbows visible, and uninterrupted pipes. Production promotion and the approval marker
   remain unset. Camera landmarks cannot independently prove physical contact with a floor or bar.
2. **RevenueCat credentials:** Flap Fit project `proja58d3dbd` has Ads access
   (dashboard URL segment `a58d3dbd`; full ID verified in Project Settings). The App Store registration
   still needs its private Apple key upload and public iOS SDK key. The Android configuration
   `app5d011c6989` is saved and its public SDK key is wired into all three EAS profiles.
   Google purchase-service credentials were not created or uploaded; no purchase products exist.
   Apple shows original key `5QBW7NBXRG` as downloaded, but no local private .p8 was recovered.
   Replacement-key creation was rejected by automatic approval review; an explicit replacement
   approval is pending. No existing key was revoked or changed.
3. **Native verification:** compile the exact final source and test consent, ad pacing/failures,
   sharing send/cancel/return, camera/audio permissions, backgrounding and repeat runs. Confirm
   RevenueCat receives real events and inspect merged privacy manifests/Android permissions.
   The private EAS simulator compile attempt was rejected before execution by automatic approval
   review because it uploads source to Expo. Explicit approval for that one private compile is
   pending. No build was started, and no signing credentials were changed.
4. **Website and consent publication:** prepared app-ads.txt and advertising policy updates need
   approval in the separate website work. Then publish matching consent messages and verify AdMob
   ownership/readiness after the store listings exist. AdMob also warns of account inactivity.
   Fresh public checks still find the obsolete no-advertising-SDK statement and no AdMob or
   RevenueCat disclosure; app-ads.txt returns the site's missing-page response. Website editing
   remains with the user's separate task, as instructed in the original handoff.
5. **Dependencies/build image:** exact patch diffs were reviewed. Sharing 57.0.20 changes metadata;
   Expo/build-properties mainly add opt-in Xcode 27 scene support. The tested app versions remain
   unchanged and iOS profiles now pin the supported Xcode 26.6 image. A simulator compile profile
   is prepared. Expo patch warnings are recorded; final native compilation is still required.
6. **Store material/account inputs:** genuine screenshots, review phone number, mailbox send/reply
   check, account agreements/compliance, final privacy/age/health/access declarations, and actual
   build testing remain. iPhone launch is first; Android remains a separate release gate.
   Apple Business now verifies the Free Apps Agreement is Active, September 13, 2026 through
   September 14, 2027. Paid Apps Agreement is New/unsigned; Apple states it is optional for free
   apps. No paid app or IAP is planned. The DSA compliance declaration is still outstanding and
   requires the owner's self-assessment and launch-region decision; no declaration or agreement
   was accepted. Private account address details are not copied into this report.
7. **Shipaton evidence:** a public US store release during the contest window and real RevenueCat
   Ads evidence are required. SDK installation alone is insufficient. No contest entry was sent.

